Z||000000||BlackARROW||12-11-2001||08:06 PM||||A month ago, I hit a sidewalk on the right side - but slowly.  Enough to have a flat tire though.  I noticed that my wheels weren't aligned anymore (something like \ / - but a little less  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  So I had that fixed with a balljoint.  <P>Now it's 2 weeks later, and my wheels are back \ / since last sunday (and my steering wheel is off on the left), and I wonder why.  Since my little "touching", I noticed that my car is pulling on the left when braking.  I checked tonight, and my left wheel's brake looks like it grips too much.  Remember I hit it on the right side.  So I guess it is not related but coincidence.  Some mechanic told me that maybe one of my caliper's piston is not going back as it is supposed to.<BR> <BR>My question are:  what do you think of my direction problem?  I just had it aligned and it's back.<P>Would there be a way to lubricates that caliper's piston, or how much for a new one?<P>What is the key size to remove the caliper?<P>Thanks to all<P>Black--&gt; Fiero 2m4 '85<BR>...getting ready for the winter rallyes!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||GTDude||12-11-2001||09:27 PM||||I think you did alot more damage than you originally thought!  Could be a crimped rh brake line causing only the lh caliper to work.  The \/....is that the top view or front view&gt;?  Sounds like a bent tie rod end if it's the top view.  At any rate...i'd have someone very knowledgeable about front ends and brakes take a look at it.<P><BR>GTDude<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||honegod||12-12-2001||04:25 AM||||the brake thing could also be the normal swelling of the inside of the flex hoses that eventually blocks off fluid flow to and from the caliper, since the break pedal generates a lot more pressure than the caliper piston the pressure in the caliper builds up.<P>it is about time for the original hoses to start frying brakes in fieros.<p>[This message has been edited by honegod (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
